164	139,490,481,824	164. Flower of Lizard's-Tail.	A naked flower of Lizard's-Tail, with no calyx or corolla: several long-stalked stamens spreading around a small pistil with curved stigmas.
165	1280,1124,1485,1590	165. Indian Corn.	A staminate flower of Indian Corn from the tassel: two narrow pointed husk-scales with three long anthers hanging on slender filaments.
166	1543,431,1716,1589	166. Indian Corn.	A pistillate flower of Indian Corn: a small ovary at the foot bearing a single very long, slender style, the silk.
167	142,1734,465,2022	167. Moonseed Flowers.	A staminate flower of Moonseed, magnified: spreading sepals and petals around a cluster of long stamens with round anthers.
168	508,1734,836,2022	168. Moonseed Flowers.	A pistillate flower of Moonseed, magnified: pointed sepals and petals around a few small pistils in the centre.
